  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Just and Equal Communities: Securing Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights - Action Aid Liberia SRHR - new strategy 2021-2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Just and Equal Communities: Securing Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet syftar till att st&#xE4;rka kvinnors och ungas m&#xF6;jligheter att h&#xE4;vda sina r&#xE4;ttigheter och f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra deras tillg&#xE5;ng till sexuella och reproduktiva h&#xE4;lso- och sjukv&#xE5;rdstj&#xE4;nster, samt st&#xE4;rka samh&#xE4;llets och ansvariga instansers f&#xF6;rm&#xE5;ga att kunna erbjuda n&#xF6;dv&#xE4;ndigt st&#xF6;d.  

Projektet har som &#xF6;vergripande m&#xE5;l att kvinnor, ungdomar och marginaliserade grupper lever i friska, s&#xE4;kra, r&#xE4;ttvisa och inkluderande samh&#xE4;llen i Liberia. Projektet kommer att implementeras p&#xE5; 30 platser i fyra l&#xE4;n i Liberia: Bong, Montserrado, Grand Gedeh och Gbarpolu. Projektet kommer att arbeta med nationella och lokala instanser f&#xF6;r att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra tillg&#xE5;ngen till s&#xE4;ker och r&#xE4;ttvis tillg&#xE5;ng till sexuella och reproduktiva h&#xE4;lsotj&#xE4;nster, samt transformera k&#xF6;nsnormer och maktrelationer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will build the agency of women and young people to assert their rights and enhance their access to comprehensive sexual and reproductive health services and build the capacity of communities and other duty bearers to support them. 

The project has an overall goal: women, young people and marginalized groups thrive in healthy, safe, equitable and inclusive communities in Liberia. It will work with 30 communities in four counties in Liberia: Bong, Montserrado, Grand Gedeh and Gbarpolu, to transform gender norms and improve power relations and work with national and local duty bearers to increase actions to improve access to safe and equitable access to sexual and reproductive health services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the intervention is that women, young people and margianalized groups thrive in healthy, safe, equitable and inclusive communities in Liberia.
The intervention aims to achieve the following results:
1. Young people and marginalized groups with capacity and information to make healthy and informed choices and decisions on their sexual and reproductive health and rights.
2. Communities demonstrate improved power relations and reduction of traditional practices and cultural beliefs that inhibit access to comprehensive SRH
3.&#xA0;Strong and effective actions taken by communities, Human Rights Defenders, civil society and social movements in holding duty bearers to account for SRH and full implementation of Maputo Protocol and other gender related policies.
4.   FGM practitioners have credible livelihood alternatives and support women and girls rights including health and girls education</narrative>
  </description>
